<ontology/use_metallurgy_tinplate/use_metallurgy_tinplate__1115__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 170" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n170> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Borax used in Metallurgy, Smelting, Brass & Tinplate: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 170"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "BORAX: (GER. DA. SW. FR. and LAT. Borax. DU. Boras. IT. Borrace, Boraso. SP. and PORT. Borrax. RUS. Bura, Borakss. POL. Boraks.) is used as a flux for metals, and enters into the composition of some of the coloured glass pastes made in imitation of gems; but its greatest use is to facilitate the soldering of the more precious metals. It is employed also as a..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
